From 2b6ab8983604c4e5ffb562bc76ed51a4e7c959c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cynthia Condra <cynthiacondra@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 04:09:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] plotPCA: apply --log2 and --rowCenter to the matrix used for
 the SVD

plot_pca bound `m = self.matrix`, replaced `m` by a row-selected copy for --ntop, and then applied --log2 (rebinding self.matrix) and --rowCenter (in place on self.matrix). The SVD ran on `m`, so --log2 never changed the result and --rowCenter only did when --ntop kept every row. Transform `m` instead.

Found in a source-level correctness audit of research software (methods and harnesses: https://github.com/cindykrafft/research-software-audit/tree/main/audits/deeptools)
